---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Wrongful Termination Guides | wrongfulterminationcalc.com"
  description="In-depth guides on wrongful termination damages, warning signs, what to do after being fired, and the at-will employment doctrine."
>

  <h1>Wrongful Termination Guides</h1>

  <p>
    Our guides go deeper than the calculator. They explain the legal concepts behind wrongful termination, help you recognize whether your situation might give rise to a claim, and walk you through the practical steps you should take after a disputed firing.
  </p>

  <div class="guide-list">

    <div class="guide-card">
      <h2><a href="/guides/how-wrongful-termination-damages-are-calculated">How Wrongful Termination Damages Are Calculated</a></h2>
      <p>
        A detailed breakdown of back pay, front pay, emotional distress awards, punitive damages, statutory caps, and how courts assess the mitigation duty. Understand the framework lawyers and judges use to put dollar figures on wrongful termination claims.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/guides/how-wrongful-termination-damages-are-calculated">Read the guide &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-card">
      <h2><a href="/guides/signs-your-termination-may-have-been-wrongful">Signs Your Termination May Have Been Wrongful</a></h2>
      <p>
        Not every unfair firing is illegal — but some are. Learn to recognize the red flags: firing after protected activity, inconsistent explanations, disparate treatment compared to coworkers, pretextual reasons, and suspicious timing around FMLA leave, pregnancy, or a complaint to HR.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/guides/signs-your-termination-may-have-been-wrongful">Read the guide &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-card">
      <h2><a href="/guides/what-to-do-after-wrongful-termination">What to Do After Wrongful Termination</a></h2>
      <p>
        A step-by-step action plan: document everything before your access is cut off, preserve key records, understand your EEOC filing deadlines, consult an attorney, comply with your mitigation duty, and think carefully before signing any severance agreement.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/guides/what-to-do-after-wrongful-termination">Read the guide &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-card">
      <h2><a href="/guides/wrongful-termination-vs-at-will-employment">Wrongful Termination vs. At-Will Employment</a></h2>
      <p>
        The at-will doctrine is widely misunderstood. This guide explains what at-will employment actually means, the major exceptions that override it, how state laws vary, and the specific situations where at-will protection does not shield an employer from liability.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/guides/wrongful-termination-vs-at-will-employment">Read the guide &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <style>
    .guide-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .guide-card { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.5rem; }
    .guide-card h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; }
    .guide-card p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  </style>

</BaseLayout>
